 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? You could start by saying you' realized how much you spend on gifts each year, how much you end up regretting, and how those regrets affect your mood. Consider experiences that you all enjoy together, like a family dinner once a month or day trip somewhere you've never been. You could still do that, just not as often. Try reducing the number of gifts per person and making them special. Start a tradition instead. Every year on your birthday, everyone gets a tiny gift that's also an experience. Your family might even start doing it themselves.",
